<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia manufacturing prices rise 0.3 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia manufacturing prices rise 0.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's manufacturing output prices rose 0.3 percent in January to be 0.5 percent up on the year, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.  </p>
<p>Manufacturing output prices (base 1988/89):</p>
<p>				    Index   mth/mth pct  yr/yr pct</p>
<p>    January		     122.0     +0.3	 +0.5</p>
<p>    December		    121.6     +0.1	 +0.2</p>
<p>    January  1996	     121.4	0.0	 +2.8</p>
<p>Note - The bureau said price increases for basic metal products, refined petroleum products and motor vehicles were were the main contributor to the rise in the index.</p>
<p>Small price falls for a range of index items partly offset the increase.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
